+.. _cli_ref_validate:
+
+validate
+========
+
+::
+
+    Usage: sqlite-utils validate [OPTIONS] PATH DBTABLE SCHEMA_FILE
+
+      Validate a table against a row schema - a JSON Schema document describing one
+      row of the table
+
+      Exits 0 if the data is clean, 1 if there are violations, 2 if the table could
+      not be validated at all.
+
+      Example:
+
+          sqlite-utils validate data.db mytable schema.json --html report.html
+
+    Options:
+      --json FILE               Write the JSON report to this file
+      --html FILE               Write the self-contained HTML report to this file
+      --limit INTEGER           Only check the first N rows - defaults to the whole
+                                table
+      --max-violations INTEGER  Keep at most this many violations in the reports -
+                                counts stay exact  [default: 1000]
+      --coerce                  Accept values that would convert cleanly, e.g. the
+                                text "123" for an integer
+      --empty-null              Treat the empty string as null
+      --full-rows               Include the whole row with each violation
+      --silent                  Don't write the summary to stdout
+      -h, --help                Show this message and exit.
+
+
