+.. _contributing_report_ui:
+
+Working on the validation report UI
+===================================
+
+The interactive HTML report produced by :ref:`sqlite-utils validate <cli_validate>`
+is written in TypeScript, in the ``frontend/`` directory. It is built into a
+single bundle at ``sqlite_utils/static/validation-report.js``, which **is
+committed to the repository** - that way ``pip install sqlite-utils`` and
+``pytest`` need neither Node nor a network connection.
+
+If you change anything under ``frontend/src``, rebuild and commit the bundle::
+
+    cd frontend
+    npm install
+    npm test          # vitest, against a DOM
+    npm run typecheck # tsc --noEmit
+    npm run build     # rewrites sqlite_utils/static/validation-report.js
+
+Python does not generate any of the report's markup or behaviour - it only
+inlines the built bundle and the report data into a skeleton, so that the
+result is one file with nothing to fetch.
+
